	"comments": [
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A `prettier-ignore` that NESTLES freezes nothing, and the pair still prints welded.",
			"start": 10,
			"end": 96
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The pair is ONE comment (nestled_block_run) whose text is no longer the directive",
			"start": 98,
			"end": 182
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " alone; independently, nestling glues a neighbour to one end of the directive, and a",
			"start": 184,
			"end": 270
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " directive only honors from its own line. Both readings agree, and so does prettier,",
			"start": 272,
			"end": 358
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " whose own merge loses the directive text the same way — so there is no spelling in",
			"start": 360,
			"end": 445
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " which merging changes what tsv freezes.",
			"start": 447,
			"end": 489
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The directive opens the pair.",
			"start": 492,
			"end": 524
		},
		{
			"type": "Block",
			"value": " prettier-ignore\n ",
			"start": 526,
			"end": 549
		},
		{
			"type": "Block",
			"value": "* c\n",
			"start": 549,
			"end": 559
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The directive closes it.",
			"start": 581,
			"end": 608
		},
		{
			"type": "Block",
			"value": "* c\n ",
			"start": 610,
			"end": 620
		},
		{
			"type": "Block",
			"value": " prettier-ignore\n",
			"start": 620,
			"end": 643
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Control - the same multi-line directive alone still freezes its statement.",
			"start": 665,
			"end": 742
		},
		{
			"type": "Block",
			"value": " prettier-ignore\n ",
			"start": 744,
			"end": 767
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Control - a newline between the two, so nothing merges, nothing is glued, and the",
